hem  [Music]  might be you know strung out on the  streets somewhere you know i mean i  don't know but  right now i'm i'm kind of i'm kind of  lone wolf in it right now you know so  especially because a lot of the things  that i've seen having people with me you  know so i just don't wanna  you know the street side is a horrible  place you know i mean it can be a  horrible place man it's really hostile  out there  definitely there's things they don't  tell you there's things you don't see on  the news you know  like  it's pretty messed up  are you still in contact with your  family  my family uh yeah yeah i speak to my  family still absolutely  you know  they don't know that i'm uh out on the  streets right now but  other than that you know  they're doing good  my mom just bought her first house so  i'm pretty proud for that you know  what are you afraid of what do you worry  about now  right now i'm just  i'm just uh i'm worried about if i'm  gonna uh  if i'm ever gonna get the opportunity to  uh  get off the streets you know because uh  some people just don't make it you know  and i want to have a life  you know that's that's that's what i'm  worried about you know because it it'll  take its toll i know it will if i don't  do anything you know it'll take its toll  and  eventually it does man  i've seen it happening you know i see  i've met a few people and they're not  around anymore  so  [Music]  if you had your life to live all over  again bradley what would you have done  differently  if i had my life to live over again i  probably would have uh  [Music]  i would have finished school for sure  um i would i would probably be in  college right now or hopefully  you know um  i would do it way different you know  there's things that i seen that i wish i  could unsee  you know  that's what that's what gets me the most  man is the things that i i can't unsee  that's the worst part about it  what have you learned from your years  train hopping  being on the street  um